 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Howe'er the love resists,\nThe spirit of Love resides,\nTo inspire its youth to continue,\nTo bless it in eternity. And\nIt lingers, and thrills and lingers,\nAnd throbs, as if alive,\nTill from some dusky shade or shadows,\nGod, at last, will break them away.\n1856. (After \"The Song of the Poet.\") The\nOriginal is a seven-line verse,\nBut not quite well balanced: three above,\nAnd four below; again,",
